[INFO] Review Feedback: The implementation covers the core draft functionality well but has several issues: 1. In getArticle function, the condition checks article.authorId but this field is not included in the select statement, which will cause a runtime error. The function should include authorId in the select or use a different approach to check ownership. 2. The frontend Editor component has a logic flaw: when editing an existing article, it always calls publishDraft instead of checking the current published state. This means editing a draft will always publish it, which is incorrect behavior. The component should check if the article is already published and call the appropriate method. 3. The common.js reducer redirects to '/' for drafts, but it would be better UX to redirect to the editor or a drafts list page so users can continue working on their drafts. 4. Missing functionality: There is no way for users to view their drafts list or distinguish between drafts and published articles in the UI. The requirement states users should be able to save articles as drafts, but there's no mechanism to list or manage drafts separately. 5. The getArticle access control logic is incomplete - it should explicitly check if the requesting user is the author when the article is unpublished, rather than relying on authorId which isn't selected.
